# RAG accuracy/retest/review reports — generated audit output, not source.
# Regenerated per evaluation run, quote long stretches of corpus text, and go
# stale the moment retrieval changes, so they are worth reading once and not
# worth versioning. Same reasoning as app/eval/ above.
# Patterns stay prefix-anchored on the tool name but are widened here so a
# report named after the matter instead ("hyden_lexus_retest_questions.md")
# cannot slip past them the way "eval_dataset 998.jsonl" once did.
rag_accuracy_report*.md
rag_retest_*.md
rag_review*.*
rag_top90_review.xlsx
*retest*.md
*ground_truth*
*_audit_report*.md

# Session/corpus CSV exports and their apply scripts — straight database dumps
# (pages, embeddings, metadata) used to move a wiki session between machines.
# Bulk generated data, regenerable from the source DB, and large enough to
# bloat the repo; embeddings in particular are megabytes of float text.
*_delta/
sync_export/
*/pages.csv
*/page_metadata.csv
*/page_embeddings_azure.csv

# Debug output
app/debug_raw_answer.txt
app/test_output.txt
app/ingest_remaining.py
app/register_files.py



# One-off diagnostic/scratch scripts (leading-underscore convention used for
# throwaway repro/verify/trace scripts during live debugging sessions —
# reusable utilities like reingest_missing_docs.py don't use this prefix)
app/_*.py

